# Chapters & Co. - Full Stack Bookshop

A modern, full-stack e-commerce platform for books built with **Node.js, Express, and MongoDB**. This project features a customer-facing shop and a secure Admin Dashboard for inventory management.

## 🚀 Live Demo
bookshop-flame.vercel.app

## ✨ Features

### Customer Features
- **Browse Books:** Real-time product fetching from MongoDB.
- **User Authentication:** Secure Register and Login system.
- **Shopping Cart:** Add/remove items with persistent storage (LocalStorage).
- **Orders:** Place orders and view order history.

### Admin Features
- **Admin Dashboard:** Private access for authorized users.
- **Inventory Management:** Add new books or delete existing ones.
- **User Insights:** View the most recently registered users.

## 🛠️ Tech Stack
- **Frontend:** HTML5, CSS3, JavaScript (Vanilla), Bootstrap 5.
- **Backend:** Node.js, Express.js.
- **Database:** MongoDB Atlas (Mongoose).
- **Deployment:** Vercel.

## 📦 Project Structure
```text
/
├── api/                # Vercel serverless functions (if applicable)
├── models/             # Mongoose Schemas (User, Product, Order)
├── public/             # Frontend files
│   ├── admin/          # Admin Dashboard HTML
│   ├── css/            # Stylesheets
│   ├── js/             # Frontend Logic (auth, main, cart, admin)
│   └── index.html      # Main Entry Point
├── routes/             # API Endpoints (users, products, orders)
├── server.js           # Main Express Server
└── vercel.json         # Deployment configuration


## Setup Instructions
Follow these steps to set up the project locally:

1. intall all packages
 
- Install Node.js
- A MongoDB Atlas account

2. Clone the Repository

git clone https://github.com/DC-BSU-RAK/assignment-100-tomorrow-s-web-AY456309.git

cd bookshop

3. Install Dependencies
npm install

4. Environment Variables
Create a .env file in the root directory and add the following:

MONGO_URI=your_mongodb_atlas_connection_string
SESSION_SECRET=your_secret_key
PORT=3000 

Note: When deploying to Vercel, add these keys under Settings > Environment Variables.

## 5. Run the App

npm start

Open http://localhost:3000 in your browser.
